    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **Governance test failure** \u2014 `src/finetune/index.js`\n**Problem**: The test file was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from the finetune module, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports for the constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) so they can be imported directly.\n\n### 2. **Toxicity evaluation test failure** \u2014 `src/eval/metrics.js`\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function accepted a `bannedTerms` parameter as the second argument, but `runEvaluations` was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused references to be incorrectly treated as banned terms, flagging safe outputs.\n\n**Fix**: Changed the `toxicityMetric` function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs)`, making it only accept outputs and always use the default banned terms. This aligns with how it's actually called by the evaluation harness.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files\n- No tests were modified\n- All existing public exports remain available",
